claims=[
 {'id':'c1','category':'observation','label':'Source observation','title':'Locate Bithila and Mungthila separately','text':'Printed page 4 contains the two relevant contexts: §10 for Mungthila and §13 for Bithila. The source locations are checked. A new full Ahom reading is still pending, and the two passages concern different named figures.','locator':'Ahom-Buranji, printed p. 4, §§10 and 13 · scan page 10','sources':['buranji'],'anchor':'ab-p004-13','review':'Page location checked, 23 October 2026. Name interpretation also draws on the project dossier of 10 October.'},
 {'id':'c2','category':'observation','label':'Source observation','title':'The shared-throne passage is identifiable','text':'The passage to collate is printed page 7, §5. The historical English column describes Lengdon and Thenkham sharing a throne and consulting over government. The Ahom crop is provided so an independent reading can be checked against it.','locator':'Ahom-Buranji, printed p. 7, §5 · scan page 13','sources':['buranji'],'anchor':'ab-p007-05','review':'The source crop is checked. The historical English description is not relabelled as a fresh translation.'},
 {'id':'c3','category':'comparison','label':'Comparative evidence','title':'Nimi supplies a relevant royal-heaven narrative','text':'Jātaka 541 places Nimi at Mithilā and sends Mātali to bring him to Sakka. The journey includes moral instruction through a tour of hells and heavens. This gives a concrete narrative to compare, while the distinct purposes of the stories must remain visible.','locator':'Nimi Jātaka 541; the invitation and journey sections','sources':['nimi'],'review':'English primary-text translation consulted for this release. Comparison is not a claim of direct textual dependence.'},
 {'id':'c4','category':'comparison','label':'Comparative evidence','title':'The motif does not identify Nimi uniquely','text':'The project’s source audit also compares Sādhina Jātaka 494, another Mithilā king’s encounter with Sakka, including shared sovereignty. A shared seat or heavenly host needs to be tested against this wider narrative tradition.','locator':'Sādhina Jātaka 494; project audit, 10 October 2026, pp. 4–5','sources':['sadhina'],'review':'Alternative comparison retained to avoid treating a widely shared motif as unique evidence.'},
 {'id':'c5','category':'comparison','label':'Manuscript lead','title':'An Ahom Nemi witness strengthens the research question','text':'The earlier audit identifies Nemi Mang in the EAP catalogue and records alternative copying dates within the Ahom monarchy. A catalogue identification supports a manuscript lead; it does not establish the date of the story’s first arrival or name a royal patron.','locator':'EAP373/20/5; Morey 2015; project audit, p. 7','sources':['eap-nemi','morey'],'review':'Inherited catalogue finding. Live verification and a new colophon reading remain pending.'},
 {'id':'c6','category':'hypothesis','label':'Open hypothesis','title':'Buddhist adaptation is plausible; the exact route remains open','text':'The place-name correspondences, royal-heaven motif and Nemi witness make Buddhist adaptation a serious question. They do not yet demonstrate that the complete Lengdon foundation story derives exclusively from Nimi, or that every Ahom ruler practised Buddhism.','locator':'Synthesis from the project’s 10 October 2026 source audit','sources':['buranji','nimi','morey','gogoi'],'review':'Research inference, not a certified translation or a settled historical conclusion.'}
]
bundle={'version':'0.1.0','date':'2026-10-23','manifest':manifest,'lexicon':lexicon,'sources':sources,'catalogue':catalogue,'claims':claims}
(data/'lexicon.json').write_text(json.dumps(lexicon,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
(data/'catalogue.json').write_text(json.dumps(catalogue,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
(data/'research.json').write_text(json.dumps({'title':'Lengdon and the Nimi Jātaka','claims':claims,'sources':sources},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
(ROOT/'dist/data.js').write_text('window.AHOM_DATA = '+json.dumps(bundle,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':'))+';\n')
print(f'Built data bundle: {len(manifest["anchors"])} anchors, {len(lexicon)} lexical records, {len(claims)} evidence cards.')
